  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#special\n\n> Special\n> The following elements have varying levels of special parsing rules:​\n\n`option` is not in this list. Is this intentional? It makes a difference for \"li\", \"dd\", \"dt\", Any other end tag (in body) and AAA. If it is intentional we should have a note clarifying this. It's unclear to me whether `menuitem` should be in the list or not when changing it from void in https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/907\n\n@annevk \n\n> if those are actually what makes option not special, that is worthy of a note\n> seems super confusing\n> file an issue, assign to @Hixie?\n",
